As an AI language model, I do not have personal beliefs, but I can share some information about multitasking efficiency and advantages, as well as its disadvantages.

Multitasking can be effective in managing multiple priorities, but it also has its limitations. Here are some advantages and disadvantages of adopting a multitasking approach:

Advantages:
1. Increased productivity: Multitasking enables individuals to work on multiple tasks simultaneously to get more done within the same timeframe. 
2. Enhanced time management: By splitting your attention between different tasks, you can maximize your time usefully and meet multiple deadlines without compromising quality;
3. Increased skill development: Multitasking helps you enhance your coordination and develop the capability to switch between tasks promptly;
4. Improved learning and retention: When you work on multiple tasks, you tend to learn and retain more information because of the brain's cognitive stimulation; 

Disadvantages:
1. Reduced efficiency: While multitasking may seem like an effective way to complete tasks quickly, studies indicate that it reduces efficiency and increases the likelihood of errors;
2. Lack of focus: Jumping between different tasks can cause an individual to lose focus, resulting in mistakes or incomplete work;
3. Increased stress: Multitasking produces stress on the brain and may cause burnout in some individuals;
4. Decreased creativity: Working on multiple tasks simultaneously can inhibit creativity and creative problem-solving capabilities.

Overall, whether multitasking is effective in managing multiple priorities depends on personal preference and skill set. It is noteworthy that avoiding multitasking altogether is not always the best option. Adopting a task-switching model between 2-3 activities at a time for an appropriate time duration might lead to better productivity than a full-blown multitasking approach.

